From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dhtmled: the table commands and the DEInsertTableParam/DEGetBlockFmtNamesParam objects (9607)

HTML editors built on the DHTML Editing Control insert and edit tables
with TriEdit's commands: DECMD_INSERTTABLE with a DEInsertTableParam
(NumRows, NumCols, TableAttrs, CellAttrs, Caption), DECMD_INSERTROW/
INSERTCOL/INSERTCELL, DELETEROWS/DELETECOLS/DELETECELLS, MERGECELLS and
SPLITCELL; DECMD_GETBLOCKFMTNAMES fills a DEGetBlockFmtNamesParam's Names.
The commands were not supported and the two classes did not exist. The
commands now work on the live document (tables.c): the table goes where
the selection is; a row is inserted above the selection's row, a column
left of its column, a cell before its cell; MERGECELLS joins the selected
cells of a row (their contents and column spans), SPLITCELL makes a cell
two (the cells of its column in the other rows span both). QueryStatus
gives them disabled outside a table cell. The two parameter classes are
registered from the type library (their interfaces are added to
dhtmled.idl with the documented DISPIDs).
